#!/bin/sh
# The tour. busybox ash ships a "help" builtin that wins over PATH, so this is reached
# through the help() function in /etc/profile.d/bonzi.sh.
cat <<'HELP'

BONZI BUDDY - things worth trying

  bonzi                    wisdom, dispensed at random
  cat chess_openings.txt   my opening repertoire, annotated
  cat README.TXT           what you are actually running
  cat /etc/motd            the greeting, again
  uname -a                 proof
  ps aux                   real processes, doing real nothing
  rm -rf /                 I dare you. It grows back.

Anything else: Bad command or file name.
(A lie. It is Linux, so it will tell you the truth instead.)

HELP
